 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S443-025\",\n \"clauses\": {\"determine\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F10\", \"template\": \"Determine the total value of {desc}:\", \"reasoning\": \"F10 prints the verb 'Determine' with the value question, and its desc slot nests the pile families F19 and F20, so it produces problems that ask the learner to determine a value.\"},\n \"write_value\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"What is the total value of {desc}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 asks for the total value of the described money. The only answer text the packet prints is the option letter (F05, F07), so the 'write' part is not shown by any printed family; the value-asking question is the closest producible form.\"},\n \"number_of_bills\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"{count} {face} {unit}\", \"reasoning\": \"F17 prints a count of one denomination with the unit 'bill' or 'bills' (unit domain members include bill and bills), which is a number of bills. Its count domain is 1 to 12.\"},\n \"number_of_coins\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"{count} {face} {unit}\", \"reasoning\": \"F17 prints a count of one denomination with the unit 'coin' or 'coins' (unit domain members include coin and coins), which is a number of coins.\"},\n \"combination_of_bills_and_coins\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F20\", \"template\": \"{v} and {v2}\", \"reasoning\": \"F20 joins two piles from F17, and each pile's unit is chosen independently, so one problem can show a pile of bills and a pile of coins together.\"},\n \"up_to_1000\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F08\", \"template\": \"Use coins and bills to make exactly ₱{total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The total key is printed up to 1000 (printed_runs ends at 1000), so F08 produces amounts up to ₱1000.\"},\n \"centavo_coins_only\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"{count} {face} {unit}\", \"reasoning\": \"F17's face domain includes F18 (centavo faces, denom members 25 and 50, printed with the cent sign), so F17 can produce piles of centavo coins.\"},\n \"peso_coins_only\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"{count} {face} {unit}\", \"reasoning\": \"F17's face domain includes F21 (peso faces with the peso sign), and its unit can be coin or coins, so F17 can produce piles of peso coins.\"},\n \"peso_bills_only\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F17\", \"template\": \"{count} {face} {unit}\", \"reasoning\": \"F17's face domain includes F21 (peso faces) and its unit can be bill or bills, so F17 can produce piles of peso bills.\"},\n \"combined_peso_coins_and_peso_bills\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F20\", \"template\": \"{v} and {v2}\", \"reasoning\": \"F20 combines two F17 piles with independently chosen units and peso faces, so one problem can show peso coins and peso bills together.\"}\n },\n \"failing_families\": [\"F02\", \"F03\", \"F06\", \"F11\", \"F13\", \"F15\", \"F17\"],\n \"failing_templates\": [\"Step {v}: Add {peso_label}{amt} → running total = {peso_label}{running}.\", \"The total is {peso_label}{total}.\", \"The dot is at ₱{a} and it moves {direction} ₱{b}. Which amount will the dot land on?\", \"Find the total amount of {desc}, in centavos:\", \"How much is {desc} altogether, in centavos?\", \"What is the total value of {desc}, in centavos?\", \"{count} {face} {unit}\"],\n \"overall\": \"FAIL\",\n \"reasoning\": \"F17 ('{count} {face} {unit}') is the root fault. Its count (1 to 12) and its unit (bill/bills, coin/coins) are chosen independently of its face, and the face domain includes peso faces (F21) such as 100, 200 and 500 and centavo faces (F18) of 25 and 50. So the family can print a unit that does not exist for that denomination, and a unit that disagrees with the count (singular unit with a count above 1, or plural with 1). Its count is also unbounded against the ₱1000 limit, since 12 pieces of the 500 face total far more than 1000. Every family that nests F17 (F10 through F16, F19, F20) prints that text. F02 and F03 print the peso label before every amount and total, but amounts include 5, 25 and 50 and totals include 2 and 7, which are centavo values in this centavo context, so a learner reads them as pesos. F06 prints the peso sign before amounts including 25, and it can move back by more than the starting amount, which gives a negative landing value; it is also a number-line story that is outside the bills-and-coins competency. F11, F13 and F15 ask for the value in centavos. Conversion to centavos is not named by the competency, and a peso total up to 1000 becomes a centavo number well beyond grade 2 (the number format is no commas up to 1000). F04 prints the amounts as bare numbers with no unit, but the packet does not show what its computed text contains, so it is not failed here. Rule 2 is satisfied for all ten clauses.\"}",
